        "id": 1305927
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-12-20T18:34:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "What if the source PDO advertises a higher fixed capability?",
      "revId": "57de95b038ca9db52b9d44e83b481eb31f103731",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "885f8017_f13ead26",
        "filename": "zephyr/emul/tcpc/emul_tcpci_partner_snk.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 207,
      "author": {
        "id": 1511343
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-12-21T16:01:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is to catch situation, when any other source PDO is not satisfying, then vSafe5V is selected. If sink has higher capability bit set it means that it cannot provide all functionalities with 5V voltage. So if sink selects 5V PDO and has higher capability it means that it couldn\u0027t find other (satisfying) PDO in source capabilities.",
      "parentUuid": "410f1378_89252984",
      "revId": "57de95b038ca9db52b9d44e83b481eb31f103731",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "eb0fa298_ffce9672",
        "filename": "zephyr/emul/tcpc/emul_tcpci_partner_snk.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 207,
      "author": {
        "id": 1305927
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-12-21T18:18:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "But it looks like this code will set mismatch even if a higher capability fixed PDO that would have satisfied the full requirement was ultimately selected. It seems like mismatch should only be set in the case above where the sink PDO current is higher than the source PDO current.",
      "parentUuid": "885f8017_f13ead26",
      "revId": "57de95b038ca9db52b9d44e83b481eb31f103731",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "568b711d_5580c016",
        "filename": "zephyr/emul/tcpc/emul_tcpci_partner_snk.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 207,
      "author": {
        "id": 1511343
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-12-22T15:22:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Correct me if I am wrong, but only sink PDO for 5V can have higher capability bit set. It is mandatory for sink to have PDO for 5V, but at the same time the sink may require higher voltage to have full functionality. So if the sink requires higher voltage, it cannot be satisfied with any amount of current provided by source with 5V. This \u0027if statement\u0027 will set mismatch flag only when someone wants to construct RDO for 5V and sink has higher capability bit set.",
      "parentUuid": "eb0fa298_ffce9672",
      "revId": "57de95b038ca9db52b9d44e83b481eb31f103731",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
